w I'm setting up validation that tracks both fields independently, using a helper method to check if an integer value is valid—period must be at least 1, and digits must also be at least 1.\n\nWriting validation logic... Handling input validation for period and digits fields, checking if the text is empty or can be parsed as an integer. Then updating the save button state based on whether all required fields are valid, and applying the same validation logic when the period field changes.\n\nNow I'm reconsidering the validation rules—the original issue is specifically about empty strings and zero values being invalid, so I need to make sure the validation catches those cases properly. I need to reconsider the validation approach to be as minimal as possible while still preventing the crash. The bug report suggests disabling the Save button when invalid values are detected, but I think a cleaner solution is to validate inputs before parsing and apply sensible defaults if they're invalid, or just prevent the crash by checking validity first.\n\nSetting up the validation logic... I need to add validation for both the period and digits inputs, then write out the complete fixed file with the proper TextWatcher implementation that checks if these fields contain valid values before allowing the save action.\n\nWriting the validation logic... Writing the dialog setup... I'm setting up a TextWatcher to validate that both the label and secret fields are filled in before enabling the save button, then attaching it to both input fields so the button state updates in real-time as the user types.\n\nNow I need to verify that `periodInput` and `digitsInput` are properly initialized before adding the watcher—let me trace through the view setup to make sure those EditText references are available at the point where I'm adding the listeners. I'm checking the initialization order in the dialog setup, and I can see that both input fields are created before the TextWatcher is added, so that's not actually an issue—the code structure is fine. Now I need to write out the corrected version with proper input validation for the period field.\n\nDefining the validation logic... Writing the text watcher... Writing the watcher setup...\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
